Z||000000||mshill||10-14-2001||09:32 PM||||I am going to be starting on my sons 85SE restoration soon.  Currently, it has a V6 from a pontiac 6000 that was obviously not installed properly.  I have another V6 from an 85 GT that is going into it.  I am also replacing all the body panels and front and rear fascias.<P>I have a set of Aero fascias from an 86SE (ribbed molding, dual outlets), and a set of fascias from an 87 coupe (round molding, single exhaust outlet).  My dillema is this: If I use the Aero Fascias, I don't have the fender and doors with the ground effects, but if I user the 87 Coupe fascias (I have all of the round molding and marker lights) I am stuck with the single exhaust outlet.<P>Is the L4 exhaust the same diameter as the V6 from the downpipe back?  The idea of a single exhaust with a custom oval tip would look sweet, but I just want to know if anyone is using the L4 exhaust with a V6 without adverse affects.||||reg||1
